# The Glutton's "exile up to two target cards from graveyards" is one simultaneous exile (CR 101.4, 608.2), so Hardened Academic's
# "whenever one or more cards leave your graveyard" (CR 603.2c, 603.10a) triggers once, not once per card: one +1/+1 counter.
# Turn 1: Academic, an Ornithopter and a Shock that kills it (graveyard: Ornithopter, Shock). The Trespasser (turn 3) enters with
# no target; night comes on turn 7 (Bot2 casts nothing on turn 6), and the attacking Glutton exiles both cards.
# The Ornithopter is the one creature card, so the drain is 1 (20 - 1 - 4 = 15).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Shock
Hardened Academic
Graveyard Trespasser
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hardened Academic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Shock.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Graveyard Trespasser.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
? DayNight = Night
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hardened Academic.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Graveyard Glutton > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Graveyard.Ornithopter; Bot1.Graveyard.Shock)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Hardened Academic)
[T7 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter; Shock
Bot1.Battlefield.Hardened Academic.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot2.Life = 15
